    "**Are the test MSEs inside the CV error bars, and should they be?** All\n",
    "of them come out *below* their cross-validated estimates, the one-layer\n",
    "networks by two to three of their standard errors, and this is neither\n",
    "luck nor a mistake — it is exercise 1a. The two-layer network of c)\n",
    "reaches $0.0116$, within about one test-set standard deviation of the\n",
    "noise floor $\\sigma^2=0.0100$: on this test set there is essentially\n",
    "nothing left to learn. The CV estimate describes the procedure trained on 80\n",
    "points; the test MSE describes the single model refitted on all 100, which\n",
    "is a better model, and on a smooth one-dimensional problem twenty-five per\n",
    "cent more data is worth a visible amount. Two effects push the other way —\n",
    "the downward bias of a selected minimum (1d), and the fact that the\n",
    "standard error $s/\\sqrt k$ is itself optimistic (1b) — and here they lose\n",
    "to the refit. There is also a third source of scatter that none of the\n",
    "error bars contain: the test set is itself a sample of 100 noisy points,\n",
    "whose MSE has a standard deviation of about $0.0014$ even for a perfect\n",
    "model, so two test sets with different seeds would disagree by that much.\n",
    "So, no, the test MSE need not be inside the CV error bar, and when it is\n",
    "not, the direction and the size of the discrepancy are what the numbers\n",
    "say about the refit, the selection and the sample — not about the\n",
    "correctness of the cross-validation. What *must* hold is that every\n",
    "decision was taken before the test set was opened, and that it was opened\n",
    "once; and it was."
   ]
