    "## Exercise 3 (optional): the MNIST classifier of Project 2, part e)\n",
    "\n",
    "The same wrapper with `ClassifierMixin`. `fit` stores the sorted labels in\n",
    "`self.classes_` (every `scikit-learn` classifier has this attribute, and\n",
    "`cross_val_predict` and `GridSearchCV` with `scoring=\"accuracy\"` rely on\n",
    "it), one-hot encodes the labels, and trains the week-41 network with the\n",
    "softmax head; `predict_proba` returns the class probabilities and\n",
    "`predict` the label with the largest one. The data are the official\n",
    "training set, the pixels scaled to $[0,1]$; everything but the last step\n",
    "uses a stratified subset of $10\\,000$ images, $1000$ per digit, in random\n",
    "order (the order matters for `learning_curve`, which takes the *first*\n",
    "$m$ training samples of every fold). `StratifiedKFold` keeps the ten\n",
    "proportions in every fold; with 1000 of each digit it gives exactly 200\n",
    "per digit in every validation fold."
   ]
  },
