   "source": [
    "def kfold_indices(n, k, seed):\n",
    "    \"\"\"The folds of KFold(k, shuffle=True, random_state=seed): a RandomState permutation cut into k contiguous blocks.\"\"\"\n",
    "    perm = np.random.RandomState(seed).permutation(n)\n",
    "    sizes = np.full(k, n // k); sizes[:n % k] += 1\n",
    "    bounds = np.r_[0, np.cumsum(sizes)]\n",
    "    folds = []\n",
    "    for i in range(k):\n",
    "        val = np.sort(perm[bounds[i]:bounds[i + 1]])\n",
    "        folds.append((np.setdiff1d(np.arange(n), val), val))\n",
    "    return folds\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def cross_validate_by_hand(make_model, X, y, folds, scale=True):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One validation and one training MSE per fold; the scaler is fitted on the training part of each fold only.\"\"\"\n",
    "    val_scores, train_scores = [], []\n",
    "    for train_idx, val_idx in folds:\n",
    "        X_tr, X_val = X[train_idx], X[val_idx]\n",
    "        if scale:\n",
    "            mean, std = X_tr.mean(axis=0), X_tr.std(axis=0)\n",
    "            X_tr, X_val = (X_tr - mean) / std, (X_val - mean) / std\n",
    "        model = make_model().fit(X_tr, y[train_idx])\n",
    "        val_scores.append(mse(y[val_idx], model.predict(X_val)))\n",
    "        train_scores.append(mse(y[train_idx], model.predict(X_tr)))\n",
    "    return np.array(val_scores), np.array(train_scores)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "folds = kfold_indices(n, k, 2026)\n",
    "print(\"same folds as KFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=2026):\",\n",
    "      all(np.array_equal(v, v_sk) and np.array_equal(t, t_sk) for (t, v), (t_sk, v_sk) in zip(folds, cv.split(X))))\n",
    "val_h, train_h = cross_validate_by_hand(lambda: NeuralNetRegressor(hidden=(50,), gamma=0.03, epochs=1000), X, y, folds)\n",
    "print(f\"by hand:      CV MSE {val_h.mean():.5f} +/- {se(val_h):.5f}, training {train_h.mean():.5f}, folds {np.round(val_h, 5)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"exercise 2a:  CV MSE {first['mean']:.5f} +/- {first['se']:.5f}, training {first['train'].mean():.5f}, folds {np.round(first['val'], 5)}\")\n",
    "print(\"identical:\", np.allclose(val_h, first[\"val\"]) and np.allclose(train_h, first[\"train\"]))\n",
    "# and the grid of 2b in miniature, with two loops instead of GridSearchCV\n",
    "small = np.zeros((2, 2))\n",
    "for i, g in enumerate([0.03, 0.1]):\n",
    "    for j, l in enumerate([0.0, 1e-4]):\n",
    "        small[i, j] = cross_validate_by_hand(lambda g=g, l=l: NeuralNetRegressor(hidden=(50,), gamma=g, lmbd=l, epochs=1000), X, y, folds)[0].mean()\n",
    "print(\"the 2x2 corner of the grid of 2b, by hand:\\n\", np.round(small, 5))\n",
    "print(\"GridSearchCV gave:\\n\", np.round(grid_mse[np.ix_([3, 4], [0, 2])], 5), \"\\nidentical:\", np.allclose(small, grid_mse[np.ix_([3, 4], [0, 2])]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7845dc08",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "That is all `cross_validate` and `GridSearchCV` do: a permutation cut\n",
    "into $k$ pieces, a scaler fitted $k$ times, a model trained $k$ times from\n",
    "scratch, and the $k$ numbers summarised. Knowing this is what lets you read\n",
    "`cv_results_` without guessing (what `std_test_score` is, why the folds\n",
    "have to be fixed before the comparison, what `best_estimator_` was trained\n",
    "on), and it is what you will need the day the problem does not fit the\n",
    "library's assumptions — grouped samples, a time series, a model that is\n",
    "trained once and evaluated at every epoch, as in exercise 2d.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Insights, with the numbers behind them\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **The CV error is the error of a procedure on $n(k-1)/k$ points, not\n",
    "   of the model you keep.** The chosen network's test MSE lands\n",
    "   *below* its CV estimate (2f), because the refit on all 100 points is a\n",
    "   better model than the fold models on 80, and that is expected.\n",
    "2. **Fix the folds first, compare on the same folds.** All comparisons in\n",
    "   this notebook — 25 grid points, five widths, seven architectures, six\n",
    "   epoch counts, fifteen degrees — use one `KFold` object, so the\n",
    "   fold-to-fold variation (a factor of three between the five folds in 2a)\n",
    "   partly cancels in every difference.\n",
    "3. **$s/\\sqrt k$ is optimistic and $k$ does not buy precision** (1b): fold\n",
    "   errors sharing $3/4$ of their training data are not independent, the\n",
    "   real spread of the estimate stops shrinking at $k=5$, and the claimed\n",
    "   standard error sits below it. Use it to compare on the same folds, not\n",
    "   to certify a number.\n",
    "4. **The scaler goes inside the fold**, and the `Pipeline` puts it there\n",
    "   for free (1c); for OLS on polynomial features the leak happens to be\n",
    "   invisible, for the network it is not.\n",
    "5. **Choosing on the test set destroys it.** The best of ten equally good\n",
    "   models reports $0.0079$ for a true $0.0100$ (1d); the same bias sits on\n",
    "   the best cell of any grid and on the dip of a per-epoch validation\n",
    "   curve (2d), which is why the test set is opened once, afterwards.\n",
    "6. **On this grid the learning rate matters, the penalty does not** (2b):\n",
    "   the minimum is on the edge of the grid at $\\gamma=0.1$, the two smallest\n",
    "   rates and the largest penalty never leave the constant predictor, and\n",
    "   the one-standard-error rule picks $\\gamma=0.1$, $\\lambda=10^{-4}$ over\n",
    "   $\\lambda=0$ because the data cannot tell them apart. The grid should be\n",
    "   extended towards larger $\\gamma$ — or the epochs increased (2d), which\n",
    "   plays the same role.\n",
    "7. **Width is not resolved, depth is** (2c): one hidden layer of 5 to 100\n",
    "   units gives the same CV MSE within the error bars, two hidden layers of\n",
    "   50 or 100 are better by three to four standard errors, and three sigmoid\n",
    "   layers of 25 do not train at all — the training MSE next to the CV MSE\n",
    "   is what shows which. The validation curve over the epochs is still\n",
    "   falling at 2000 (2d): the one-layer network underfits. Early stopping is\n",
    "   cheap when the validation error is recorded inside the training loop —\n",
    "   one run per fold, identical to `validation_curve` to every digit.\n",
    "8. **The polynomial matches the network on the Runge function** (2e): OLS\n",
    "   of degree 11 with twelve parameters, $0.0211\\pm0.0032$, beats the\n",
